{"id":"0764ea4b-a7bc-4cb6-9a8a-bbdc2f11875f","object":"chat.completion","created":1785037430,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        mr = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    size = {n: 1 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(a, b):\\n        ra = find(a)\\n        rb = find(b)\\n        if ra == rb:\\n            return\\n        if size[ra] < size[rb]:\\n            ra, rb = rb, ra\\n        parent[rb] = ra\\n        size[ra] += size[rb]\\n    mst = []\\n    total = 0.0\\n    for mr, u, v in edges:\\n        if len(mst) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n            break\\n        if find(u) != find(v):\\n            union(u, v)\\n            mst.append([u, v, mr])\\n            total += mr\\n    if len(mst) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst, 'total_weight': total}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce Python source code for solve(case) that returns a JSON object with mst_edges and total_weight. The input case payload contains nodes (list of node names), core_distance (dict mapping node to core distance), distances (list of [node1, node2, distance] lists). Need to compute mutual reachability as max(core1, core2, distance). Then build MST using Kruskal: sort edges by mutual reachability, and tie-break by node ids (canonicalize undirected endpoints: store as tuple sorted alphabetically? The instruction says \"canonicalize undirected endpoints\" and \"sort by reachabili